 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "16 is a dialogue commanded to the Prophet ﷺ («قل»): no plate starts on «قل»; geometric for «رب السماوات والأرض… الله» and «الله خالق كل شيء وهو الواحد القهار», light for «الظلمات والنور». The parable of 17 in symbols: rain cloud, river (earthly), wave for the foam, a worldly fire for smelting (as a tool), a jewel for «حلية», wind for «فيذهب جفاء», growth for «ما ينفع الناس فيمكث في الأرض», geometric for «يضرب الله». No people drawn. STAGING v4: c1 (16) stays ambient (geometric): the Prophet's ﷺ commanded words to the polytheists («قل»), the idols they took as protectors are never drawn and nobody faces an empty side; quiet over 16:1-7 and 16:38-45; plates unchanged (none starts on «قل»). c2 (17), the parable as it is seen in this world: a mountain valley by day; rain falls from 17:3 (water sent down from the sky) and stops at 17:12; the camera goes down to the valley floor for the valleys flowing (17:5), a wave plate for the foam on the torrent (17:9-11). The second parable is told in plates only (no smiths and no blaze are drawn: a large fire on the stage would read as a fire of punishment): a worldly-fire plate for what they kindle fire upon (17:13-16; both tafsirs: smelting the metals, for ornament or for tools), a jewel plate for ornament (17:18-21). Geometric for thus Allah strikes (17:24-27 camera only, 17:40 plate). A gust for the foam that vanishes (17:30), a water-drop plate for what benefits people remains in the earth (17:34-38). No growth is drawn (neither tafsir names plants here). The cover now shows the rain in the valley with the foam plate (17:9)."
